# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust the values for your machine.
# `.env` is git-ignored so no host addresses or keys are ever committed.
#
# Only variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ are inlined into the JS bundle by
# Expo. This app has no secrets: the mock server is unauthenticated and the map
# uses OpenStreetMap tiles, which need no API key.

# Base URL of the json-server mock REST API used by the sync service.
#
#   Android emulator ......... http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   iOS simulator ............ http://localhost:3000
#   Real device (same Wi-Fi) . http://<your-computer-LAN-ip>:3000
#
# Leave unset to fall back to the platform default resolved in
# src/constants/config.ts. The value can also be overridden at runtime from the
# Settings screen, which is the easiest option when testing the release APK.
EXPO_PUBLIC_MOCK_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000
